  "worked_solution": "Isolating the seventh-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-x)^{7}-8 & \\ge 5 \\\\ (3-x)^{7} & \\ge 13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the seventh root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[7]{(3-x)^{7}} & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13} \\\\ 3-x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13} \\\\ -x & \\ge \\sqrt[7]{13}-3 \\\\ x & \\le -\\sqrt[7]{13}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
